{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Div2_421C {\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String[] parts = br.readLine().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n        int a = Integer.parseInt(parts[0]);\n        int b = Integer.parseInt(parts[1]);\n        long l = Long.parseLong(parts[2]);\n        long r = Long.parseLong(parts[3]);\n\n        if (r - l + 1 >= 2L * (a + b)) {\n            System.out.println(a <= b ? a + 1 : 2 * a - b);\n            return;\n        }\n\n        l--;\n        r--;\n\n        int minDistinct = 26;\n\n        for (int first = 0; first < 26; first++) {\n            for (int second = a; second < 26; second++) {\n                List<Integer> chars = new ArrayList<>();\n                for (int i = 0; i < a; i++) chars.add(i);\n                for (int i = 0; i < b; i++) chars.add(first);\n                chars.addAll(getSuffixChars(chars.subList(chars.size() - a, chars.size())));\n                for (int i = 0; i < b; i++) chars.add(second);\n\n                int len = chars.size();\n                Set<Integer> distinct = new HashSet<>();\n                for (long i = l % len; i <= r % len; i = (i + 1) % len) {\n                    distinct.add(chars.get((int) i));\n                    if (i == r % len) break;\n                }\n                minDistinct = Math.min(minDistinct, distinct.size());\n            }\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(minDistinct);\n    }\n\n    private static List<Integer> getSuffixChars(List<Integer> lastA) {\n        Set<Integer> used = new HashSet<>(lastA);\n        List<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();\n        int next = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < lastA.size(); i++) {\n            while (used.contains(next)) next++;\n            result.add(next);\n            used.add(next++);\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <set>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nvector<int> getSuffixChars(const vector<int>& lastA) {\n    set<int> used(lastA.begin(), lastA.end());\n    vector<int> result;\n    int next = 0;\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < lastA.size(); i++) {\n        while (used.find(next) != used.end()) {\n            next++;\n        }\n        result.push_back(next);\n        used.insert(next);\n        next++;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    string line;\n    getline(cin, line);\n    \n    vector<string> parts;\n    string current = \"\";\n    for (char c : line) {\n        if (c == ' ' || c == '\\t') {\n            if (!current.empty()) {\n                parts.push_back(current);\n                current = \"\";\n            }\n        } else {\n            current += c;\n        }\n    }\n    if (!current.empty()) {\n        parts.push_back(current);\n    }\n    \n    int a = stoi(parts[0]);\n    int b = stoi(parts[1]);\n    long long l = stoll(parts[2]);\n    long long r = stoll(parts[3]);\n    \n    if (r - l + 1 >= 2LL * (a + b)) {\n        cout << (a <= b ? a + 1 : 2 * a - b) << endl;\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    l--;\n    r--;\n    \n    int minDistinct = 26;\n    \n    for (int first = 0; first < 26; first++) {\n        for (int second = a; second < 26; second++) {\n            vector<int> chars;\n            for (int i = 0; i < a; i++) chars.push_back(i);\n            for (int i = 0; i < b; i++) chars.push_back(first);\n            \n            vector<int> suffix = getSuffixChars(vector<int>(chars.end() - a, chars.end()));\n            chars.insert(chars.end(), suffix.begin(), suffix.end());\n            \n            for (int i = 0; i < b; i++) chars.push_back(second);\n            \n            int len = chars.size();\n            set<int> distinct;\n            \n            long long start = l % len;\n            long long end = r % len;\n            \n            if (start <= end) {\n                for (long long i = start; i <= end; i++) {\n                    distinct.insert(chars[i]);\n                }\n            } else {\n                for (long long i = start; i < len; i++) {\n                    distinct.insert(chars[i]);\n                }\n                for (long long i = 0; i <= end; i++) {\n                    distinct.insert(chars[i]);\n                }\n            }\n            \n            minDistinct = min(minDistinct, (int)distinct.size());\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << minDistinct << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00015948931104503572, -2.264974000354414e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.0003524397616274655, -7.152555099310121e-07, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.264974000354414e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.032704420387744904, -4.768370445162873e-07, -5.722029527532868e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0